  "guards": [
    "EUR cash flows, WACC, claims and simulation remain native EUR. Separate historical USD object is never a currency relabel.",
    "Current equity, current-price comparisons and as-known backtesting remain unavailable. Both native allocation and historical USD disappear when date or claim gate fails.",
    "Customer-advance runoff stays fixed in years 1–5 under capital factors, annual innovations, horizon extension and terminal normalization; never deducted as debt.",
    "Future economic grants remain in EBIT; legacy expense subtraction/reversal gives zero uplift. Old awards/options are allocated once.",
    "Opening tax liabilities and current tax asset are included once; no noncurrent DTA credit or repeated forecast settlement.",
    "Eight selected claim controls preserve explicit unknowns; unbounded maxima are not turned into zeros or fictitious finite limits.",
    "Research defaults are fixed and Run is manual; runoff stresses have no assigned probabilities.",
    "Source, bridge, history, report, audit, FX and timing identities are pinned. Earlier package bytes are unchanged."
  ],
